625 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 624 0 R
  /Alt (A spatial classification map overlaid on high-resolution aerial imagery, illustrating different land cover feature types and re-inclusion statuses resulting from a raster-to-vector conversion process. The map shows a mixed landscape including urbanised areas, agricultural fields, and natural/forested patches. The legend defines six feature classifications: * **Linear** (light green solid fill): Represents linear features such as field boundaries or small linear landscape elements. * **Patchy** (dark green solid fill): Represents non-linear, compact features. * **Area: Out of specs** (red hatched outline): Denotes patchy features that were outside of the defined area threshold. * **Agriculture: High coverage** (orange hatched outline): Identifies crop areas with more than 80% crop coverage. * **Re-inclusion, connected to linear or patchy** (teal/cyan solid fill): Represents features connected to valid geometries (linear or patchy features) and not covered by crops (less than 80% crop coverage). * **No re-inclusion: Agriculture** (yellow hatched outline): Indicates agricultural areas that were not re-included in the analysis. The map displays large areas of 'No re-inclusion: Agriculture' (yellow hatched) covering extensive agricultural fields, with smaller 'Agriculture: High coverage' (orange hatched) patches within them. Scattered throughout the landscape are numerous 'Linear' (light green) and 'Patchy' (dark green) features. Larger, often irregular, clusters of 'Re-inclusion, connected to linear or patchy' (teal/cyan) are visible, particularly on the left and lower central parts of the map. A single small 'Area: Out of specs' (red hatched) feature is visible near the center-left. No scale bar, compass, or specific geographic location or date are provided on the map.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [14]
  /Pg 1614 0 R
>>
endobj

